{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:FluidDynamics.RegularityBreakdown","@type":"LeanModule","name":"FluidDynamics.RegularityBreakdown","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Archimedean","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Floor.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Round","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.RegularityBreakdown.profile_not_steady","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.RegularityBreakdown.profile_not_steady","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/regularity-breakdown.lean#L107-L107","doc":"**Clause 3b — the profile is not steady.**  The `s`-independent\nself-similar profile is excluded \\[necas-ruzicka-sverak1996], so\nthe periodicity above is non-trivial. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.RegularityBreakdown.profile_periodic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.RegularityBreakdown.profile_periodic","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/regularity-breakdown.lean#L103-L103","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.RegularityBreakdown.period_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.RegularityBreakdown.period_pos","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/regularity-breakdown.lean#L102-L102","doc":"**Clause 3a — discrete, not continuous, self-similarity.**  The\nLeray profile is periodic in `s` with a genuine period. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.RegularityBreakdown.sheet_dim_eq_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.RegularityBreakdown.sheet_dim_eq_two","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/regularity-breakdown.lean#L99-L99","doc":"**Clause 2 — vortex sheet concentration.**  The vorticity\nconcentrates on a codimension-1 surface: spatial Hausdorff\ndimension exactly `2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.RegularityBreakdown.enstrophy_blowup","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.RegularityBreakdown.enstrophy_blowup","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/regularity-breakdown.lean#L94-L94","doc":"**Clause 1 — blowup of enstrophy.**  `enstrophy t → +∞` as\n`t → T⁻`: every bound `M` is exceeded arbitrarily close to `T`,\nfrom below.  Stated one-sidedly (`T - ε < t < T`), so a function\nthat is merely unbounded somewhere does not satisfy it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.RegularityBreakdown.T_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.RegularityBreakdown.T_pos","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/regularity-breakdown.lean#L89-L89","doc":"The blowup happens in finite positive time. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.RegularityBreakdown.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.RegularityBreakdown.mk","kind":"ctor","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/regularity-breakdown.lean#L86-L86","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.RegularityBreakdown","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.RegularityBreakdown","kind":"class","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/regularity-breakdown.lean#L41-L107","doc":"**Conjecture class** for `conj:regularity-breakdown`.\n\n**Rewritten 2026-08-30.**  The single field was\n\n    critical_reynolds : ∃ Re_c : ℝ, Re_c > 0\n\n— \"there exists a positive real\", a theorem of ordered fields,\ndischarged by `1`.  Two defects, not one: it was vacuous, *and* it\nwas about the wrong object.  Its docstring spoke of a critical\nReynolds number and a Sobolev `H²` bound; the `.md` conjecture\nmentions neither.  A downstream `[RegularityBreakdown]` hypothesis\nwas therefore free **and** misdescribed.\n\nThe class is now parametrised by the objects the `.md` conjecture is\nabout, and its fields are that conjecture's three numbered clauses.\n\n**Parameters.**  `enstrophy t` is `∫ |ω(x,t)|² dx`; `T` is the\nblowup time `T*`; `sheetDim` is the *spatial* Hausdorff dimension of\nthe vortex sheet; `profile s` is the solution in Leray's similarity\nvariable `s = -log(T* - t)`, and `period` is its `s`-period, set by\nthe root-of-unity scaling `λ_κ`.\n\nTwo notes on faithfulness to the `.md`.\n\n*  `sheet_dim_eq_two` records the **spatial** dimension `d_H = 2`.\n   The `.md` is explicit that this is not a priori a CKN violation —\n   CKN bounds the *parabolic* dimension of the space–time singular\n   set by `1`, a different set — and that reconciling the two is a\n   required step \"not yet carried out\".  So this class does not\n   assert the reconciliation, and it deliberately carries no\n   space–time dimension field: there is nothing derived to put in\n   one.\n*  `profile_not_steady` is the Nečas–Růžička–Šverák exclusion\n   \\[necas-ruzicka-sverak1996]: the continuous, `s`-independent\n   self-similar profile is ruled out, so the periodicity in\n   `profile_periodic` must be non-trivial.  Dropping this field\n   would let a constant `profile` satisfy the class, which is\n   exactly the case the literature excludes.\n\nThis does not prove the conjecture.  It makes assuming it mean\nsomething: each field is refutable by a wrong object, and the\nnegative controls below exhibit such objects.\n\nRef: [leitner2026] §Regularity breakdown at q = 1: the classical limit\nas a phase transition, `conj:regularity-breakdown` ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:regularity-breakdown","label":"conj:regularity-breakdown","md":"quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/regularity-breakdown.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}